1
00:00:00,668 --> 00:00:01,042
READY?
YEAH.

2
00:00:01,042 --> 00:00:02,043
OKAY.

3
00:00:02,043 --> 00:00:03,044
HI.
IT'S...

4
00:00:03,044 --> 00:00:04,171
RACHEL...
AND...

5
00:00:04,171 --> 00:00:05,547
PHOEBE'S...
PLEASE...

6
00:00:05,547 --> 00:00:06,632
LEAVE...

7
00:00:06,632 --> 00:00:08,634
LEAVE...

8
00:00:08,634 --> 00:00:10,010
WAIT, I-I JUST
SAID, "LEAVE."

9
00:00:10,010 --> 00:00:11,052
YEAH, I KNOW,
BECAUSE YOU HAVE

10
00:00:11,052 --> 00:00:13,472
ALL THE GOOD WORDS.

11
00:00:13,472 --> 00:00:14,974
WHAT DO I GET?
I GET "IT'S,"

12
00:00:14,974 --> 00:00:16,684
"AND"--
OH, I'M SORRY, I HAVE "A."

13
00:00:16,684 --> 00:00:18,393
FORGET IT.

14
00:00:18,393 --> 00:00:20,270
PHOEBE, COME ON.
THAT'S SILLY.

15
00:00:20,270 --> 00:00:21,438
ALL RIGHT,
SO, LET'S SWITCH.

16
00:00:21,438 --> 00:00:24,399
NO, I HAVE ALL
THE GOOD WORDS.

17
00:00:24,399 --> 00:00:26,735
OKAY, FINE, FINE.
WE CAN SWITCH.

18
00:00:26,735 --> 00:00:28,863
OKAY.
OKAY.

19
00:00:28,863 --> 00:00:29,864
HI...

20
00:00:29,864 --> 00:00:30,865
EVERYBODY...

21
00:00:30,865 --> 00:00:31,991
IT'S...
RACHEL...

22
00:00:31,991 --> 00:00:33,241
AND...
PHOEBE'S...

23
00:00:33,241 --> 00:00:34,242
PLEASE... WAIT.

24
00:00:34,242 --> 00:00:35,619
HOW DID YOU DO THAT?

25
00:00:35,619 --> 00:00:37,955
WHAT?

26
00:00:37,955 --> 00:00:41,583
OH... YOU'RE NO
ORDINARY ROOMMATE, ARE YOU?

27
00:00:41,583 --> 00:00:43,002
PH-PHOEBE, COME ON.
CAN WE FINISH THIS LATER?

28
00:00:43,002 --> 00:00:45,044
I WANT TO GO RUNNING
BEFORE IT GETS DARK.

29
00:00:45,044 --> 00:00:46,797
OH! WHY DON'T YOU COME WITH ME?

30
00:00:46,797 --> 00:00:48,340
REALLY?
YEAH.

31
00:00:48,340 --> 00:00:49,591
OH, IT'LL BE FUN.
WE'LL RUN IN THE PARK.

32
00:00:49,591 --> 00:00:51,218
IT'LL BE, LIKE, OUR FIRST

33
00:00:51,218 --> 00:00:53,387
YOU KNOW,
ROOMMATE-BONDING THING.

34
00:00:53,387 --> 00:00:55,096
OKAY, LET'S GO RUNNING.
YEAH...

35
00:00:55,096 --> 00:00:56,557
AND THERE'S REALLY CUTE GUYS.

36
00:00:56,557 --> 00:00:59,184
LET'S RUN TOWARDS THEM!
OKAY.

37
00:00:59,184 --> 00:01:01,436
ALL RIGHT,
WAIT JUST ONE MORE SECOND.

38
00:01:01,436 --> 00:01:02,813
HI. IT'S PHOEBE AND RACHEL'S.

39
00:01:02,813 --> 00:01:04,565
PLEASE LEAVE A MESSAGE. THANKS.

40
00:01:04,565 --> 00:01:05,566
WELL, NOW,
WAIT A MINUTE.

41
00:01:05,566 --> 00:01:07,275
YOU JUST TOOK
ALL THE WORDS.

42
00:01:07,275 --> 00:01:10,195
UH-HUH, YOU'VE MET YOUR MATCH,
RACHEL GREEN.

43
00:01:16,869 --> 00:01:21,916
♪ SO NO ONE TOLD YOU
LIFE WAS GONNA BE THIS WAY ♪

44
00:01:21,916 --> 00:01:24,001
♪ YOUR JOB'S A JOKE,
YOU'RE BROKE ♪

45
00:01:24,001 --> 00:01:26,795
♪ YOUR LOVE LIFE'S D.O.A. ♪

46
00:01:26,795 --> 00:01:31,174
♪ IT'S LIKE YOU'RE ALWAYS
STUCK IN SECOND GEAR ♪

47
00:01:31,174 --> 00:01:33,802
♪ WHEN IT HASN'T BEEN
YOUR DAY, YOUR WEEK ♪

48
00:01:33,802 --> 00:01:36,388
♪ YOUR MONTH,
OR EVEN YOUR YEAR ♪

49
00:01:36,388 --> 00:01:40,183
♪ BUT I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

50
00:01:40,183 --> 00:01:46,356
♪ 'CAUSE YOU'RE THERE
FOR ME, TOO. ♪

51
00:01:50,694 --> 00:01:53,989
SO, I JUST FINISHED
THIS FASCINATING BOOK.

52
00:01:53,989 --> 00:01:57,367
BY THE YEAR 2030,
THERE'LL BE COMPUTERS

53
00:01:57,367 --> 00:01:59,828
THAT CAN CARRY OUT
THE SAME AMOUNT OF FUNCTIONS

54
00:01:59,828 --> 00:02:02,497
AS AN ACTUAL HUMAN BRAIN.

55
00:02:02,497 --> 00:02:04,875
SO, THEORETICALLY,
YOU COULD DOWNLOAD

56
00:02:04,875 --> 00:02:08,629
YOUR THOUGHTS AND MEMORIES
INTO THIS COMPUTER

57
00:02:08,629 --> 00:02:13,968
AND-AND-AND LIVE FOREVER,
AS A MACHINE.

58
00:02:17,096 --> 00:02:21,516
AND I JUST REALIZED
I CAN SLEEP WITH MY EYES OPEN.

59
00:02:21,516 --> 00:02:22,517
( door opening )

60
00:02:22,517 --> 00:02:23,518
HEY.

61
00:02:23,518 --> 00:02:25,144
HEY.
HEY.

62
00:02:25,144 --> 00:02:27,481
HONEY, THAT'S A GREAT IDEA--
NAILING THE BOXES

63
00:02:27,481 --> 00:02:30,901
TO THE FLOOR.

64
00:02:30,901 --> 00:02:32,527
I DIDN'T NAIL THE BOXES
TO THE FLOOR.

65
00:02:32,527 --> 00:02:34,446
OH, SO YOU CAN MOVE THEM?

66
00:02:34,446 --> 00:02:36,907
YES. YES,
AND WHILE I'M DOING THAT

67
00:02:36,907 --> 00:02:39,994
ROSS HAS A GREAT COMPUTER STORY
FOR YOU.

68
00:02:42,203 --> 00:02:44,456
HEY, EVERYBODY.
UH, I'D LIKE YOU
TO MEET JANINE.

69
00:02:44,456 --> 00:02:46,333
SHE'S-SHE'S GOING TO
BE MY NEW ROOMMATE.

70
00:02:46,333 --> 00:02:48,627
HI.

71
00:02:48,627 --> 00:02:50,754
HI.
HI.

72
00:02:50,754 --> 00:02:53,590
YEAH, SHE'S GOING
TO LIVE WITH ME!

73
00:02:55,300 --> 00:02:57,176
IT'S NICE TO MEET YOU.
UH, JANINE...

74
00:02:57,176 --> 00:02:58,386
LECROIX, JANINE LECROIX.

75
00:02:58,386 --> 00:02:59,638
I DIDN'T KNOW THAT.

76
00:02:59,638 --> 00:03:02,724
WH-WHAT A PRETTY
LAST NAME.

77
00:03:02,724 --> 00:03:04,518
SO, UH, WH-WHERE
ARE YOU FROM?

78
00:03:04,518 --> 00:03:06,728
AUSTRALIA. I JUST MOVED HERE
A COUPLE OF WEEKS AGO.

79
00:03:06,728 --> 00:03:08,355
FROM THE LAND
DOWN UNDER?
YEAH.

80
00:03:08,355 --> 00:03:11,942
I DIDN'T KNOW
THAT, EITHER.

81
00:03:11,942 --> 00:03:13,610
SO, UH, WHAT, UH,
WHAT DO YOU DO?

82
00:03:13,610 --> 00:03:14,611
I'M A DANCER.

83
00:03:14,611 --> 00:03:16,655
YOU'RE A DANCER?

84
00:03:16,655 --> 00:03:19,741
SHE-SHE'S A DANCER.

85
00:03:19,741 --> 00:03:20,826
Janine:
WELL, I THINK

86
00:03:20,826 --> 00:03:22,369
I'LL GO AND... UNPACK.

87
00:03:22,369 --> 00:03:24,163
OH, HEY, LET ME.

88
00:03:24,163 --> 00:03:26,247
THANKS.
OKAY.

89
00:03:26,247 --> 00:03:29,126
( gasping ecstatically )

90
00:03:31,461 --> 00:03:32,587
JOEY...

91
00:03:32,587 --> 00:03:34,673
YEAH?

92
00:03:34,673 --> 00:03:36,050
DID YOU EVEN INTERVIEW
THIS WOMAN

93
00:03:36,050 --> 00:03:37,634
BEFORE YOU ASKED HER
TO MOVE IN?

94
00:03:37,634 --> 00:03:39,427
OF COURSE I DID.

95
00:03:39,427 --> 00:03:41,013
WHAT EXACTLY
DID YOU ASK HER?

96
00:03:41,013 --> 00:03:42,890
"WHEN CAN YOU MOVE IN?"

97
00:03:45,350 --> 00:03:49,104
THANK YOU FOR BRINGING
HER INTO OUR LIVES.

98
00:03:49,104 --> 00:03:51,106
UNBELIEVABLE.

99
00:03:51,106 --> 00:03:53,274
OH... OH, SO, YOU LIKE HER,
TOO, CHANDLER?

100
00:03:53,274 --> 00:03:56,653
HEY, LOOK AT
ALL THE BOXES.

101
00:03:56,653 --> 00:03:59,406
OH, I CANNOT WAIT
TO ASK HER OUT.

102
00:03:59,406 --> 00:04:00,991
WAIT A MINUTE, JOEY.

103
00:04:00,991 --> 00:04:03,284
JOEY, YOU CAN'T ASK HER OUT.
SHE'S YOUR ROOMMATE.

104
00:04:03,284 --> 00:04:04,995
YOU KNOW, IT'S... IT'LL
BE WAY TOO COMPLICATED.

105
00:04:04,995 --> 00:04:06,413
YEAH, YEAH, MAN,
DON'T DO IT.

106
00:04:06,413 --> 00:04:07,581
I MEAN,
IF YOU DATE HER

107
00:04:07,581 --> 00:04:10,084
THEN-THEN-THEN
I CAN'T DATE HER.

108
00:04:10,084 --> 00:04:11,793
Chandler:
ALL RIGHT,
THINK ABOUT IT.

109
00:04:11,793 --> 00:04:13,670
NOW, REMEMBER WHEN YOU WENT
OUT WITH THAT GIRL, DONNA

110
00:04:13,670 --> 00:04:15,964
AND YOU GUYS BROKE UP?
REMEMBER HOW HORRIBLE IT WAS

111
00:04:15,964 --> 00:04:18,299
WHEN YOU GUYS BUMPED INTO EACH
OTHER AT THE SUPERMARKET?

112
00:04:18,299 --> 00:04:22,721
OH, GOD, YEAH.
NOW, IMAGINE YOU LIVE...
AT THE SUPERMARKET.

113
00:04:22,721 --> 00:04:24,973
OKAY.

114
00:04:24,973 --> 00:04:26,265
NO, NO.

115
00:04:26,265 --> 00:04:28,227
OH. OH.
OH, YOU'RE RIGHT.

116
00:04:28,227 --> 00:04:29,895
I DON'T WANT THAT.
I CAN'T DATE HER.

117
00:04:29,895 --> 00:04:31,772
YEAH, AND YOU BETTER
WATCH THE FLIRTING, TOO

118
00:04:31,772 --> 00:04:34,649
BECAUSE IN SUCH
CLOSE QUARTERS...
IT COULD BE TROUBLE.

119
00:04:34,649 --> 00:04:36,193
WELL, THAT'S GOING
TO BE TOUGH, MON. I MEAN,

120
00:04:36,193 --> 00:04:39,320
IT'S HARD FOR ME TO BE AROUND
AN ATTRACTIVE WOMAN

121
00:04:39,320 --> 00:04:41,489
AND NOT FLIRT.
( chuckles )

122
00:04:41,489 --> 00:04:42,866
WELL, YOU'RE AROUND
ME ALL THE TIME

123
00:04:42,866 --> 00:04:45,452
AND YOU DON'T FLIRT.

124
00:04:45,452 --> 00:04:47,996
YOU A LITTLE SAD
ABOUT THAT, SWEETHEART?

125
00:04:53,501 --> 00:04:54,878
I HAVE TO TIE MY SHOE.
YOU GO AHEAD.

126
00:04:54,878 --> 00:04:56,713
I'LL CATCH UP.
Both:
OKAY.

127
00:05:00,092 --> 00:05:01,384
( panting )

128
00:05:01,384 --> 00:05:02,886
COME ON!
THAT'S NOT RUNNING!

129
00:05:02,886 --> 00:05:04,679
LET'S GO!

130
00:05:10,393 --> 00:05:11,645
YOU GUYS, I'M
TELLING YOU

131
00:05:11,645 --> 00:05:13,480
WHEN SHE RUNS, SHE LOOKS LIKE

132
00:05:13,480 --> 00:05:18,485
A CROSS BETWEEN KERMIT THE FROG
AND THE SIX MILLION DOLLAR MAN.

133
00:05:18,485 --> 00:05:21,238
MONICA HAD SUCH
A CRUSH ON HIM.

134
00:05:21,238 --> 00:05:22,322
( laughing )

135
00:05:22,322 --> 00:05:24,199
YEAH, SHE USED
TO KISS HIS POSTER

136
00:05:24,199 --> 00:05:26,367
EVERY NIGHT
BEFORE SHE WENT TO BED.

137
00:05:26,367 --> 00:05:28,411
OH, I USED TO DO THAT, TOO.

138
00:05:28,411 --> 00:05:29,621
DID YOU ALSO
HAVE HIS ALBUM

139
00:05:29,621 --> 00:05:31,832
IT'S NOT EASY
BEING GREEN?

140
00:05:33,541 --> 00:05:36,503
AW, MON...

141
00:05:36,503 --> 00:05:37,671
( chuckling )

142
00:05:37,671 --> 00:05:39,965
SO, PHOEBE RUNS
WEIRD, HUH?

143
00:05:39,965 --> 00:05:41,424
YEAH, YEAH, AND YOU KNOW WHAT?

144
00:05:41,424 --> 00:05:42,843
AND I KNOW SHE'S GOING
TO WANT TO RUN AGAIN.

145
00:05:42,843 --> 00:05:44,469
I JUST DON'T KNOW HOW
TO GET OUT OF IT.

146
00:05:44,469 --> 00:05:46,096
I MEAN, I LIVE WITH HER.

147
00:05:46,096 --> 00:05:47,639
WHY DON'T YOU JUST BE
STRAIGHT WITH HER?

148
00:05:47,639 --> 00:05:49,348
TELL HER THE TRUTH.

149
00:05:49,348 --> 00:05:50,892
YOU'RE RIGHT.

150
00:05:50,892 --> 00:05:53,145
YOU'RE RIGHT, I SHOULD
JUST TELL HER THE TRUTH.

151
00:05:53,145 --> 00:05:54,353
HEY.
HEY.

152
00:05:54,353 --> 00:05:55,814
HEY, PHEEBS,
MONICA TRIPPED ME.

153
00:05:55,814 --> 00:05:59,567
I DON'T THINK
I CAN EVER RUN AGAIN, EVER.

154
00:05:59,567 --> 00:06:02,403
WHY?
WHY WOULD
YOU DO THAT?

155
00:06:02,403 --> 00:06:05,032
I DON'T KNOW.

156
00:06:05,032 --> 00:06:07,826
RACHEL, I'M-I'M SORRY
THAT I HURT YOUR ANKLES.

157
00:06:07,826 --> 00:06:08,869
ANKLE.

158
00:06:08,869 --> 00:06:10,162
WE'LL SEE.

159
00:06:14,415 --> 00:06:17,252
OKAY, I AM OFFICIALLY UNPACKED.

160
00:06:17,252 --> 00:06:18,377
THANKS FOR HELPING ME, MAN.

161
00:06:19,629 --> 00:06:21,340
JOE?

162
00:06:21,340 --> 00:06:22,590
( Joey chuckling )

163
00:06:27,386 --> 00:06:30,557
WELL, I GUESS
JOEY WENT HOME.

164
00:06:30,557 --> 00:06:32,559
OH, AND LOOK,
THERE'S STILL ONE BOX

165
00:06:32,559 --> 00:06:34,477
THAT I HAVE TO UNPACK.

166
00:06:34,477 --> 00:06:35,854
( Joey laughing )

167
00:06:37,605 --> 00:06:38,690
I GOTCHA!

168
00:06:38,690 --> 00:06:40,734
( laughing )

169
00:06:40,734 --> 00:06:41,860
OH, MY GOD!

170
00:06:41,860 --> 00:06:44,946
YOU ALMOST GAVE ME
A HEART ATTACK.

171
00:06:44,946 --> 00:06:46,489
BOY, IT WAS SO
HARD NOT TO LAUGH

172
00:06:46,489 --> 00:06:48,283
I'LL TELL YOU.

173
00:06:48,283 --> 00:06:49,450
OH, HEY-HEY...

174
00:06:49,450 --> 00:06:50,451
THE PLACE LOOKS GREAT.

175
00:06:50,451 --> 00:06:51,912
YEAH, NOT BAD, RIGHT?

176
00:06:51,912 --> 00:06:53,580
MONICA'S GOING
TO BE WORKING LATE.

177
00:06:53,580 --> 00:06:56,291
SO, I'M GOING TO MAKE
THIS PLACE SPOTLESS.

178
00:06:56,291 --> 00:06:58,043
YOU KNOW WHAT ELSE
I'M GOING TO DO?

179
00:06:58,043 --> 00:06:59,460
I'M GOING
TO GO DOWNSTAIRS.

180
00:06:59,460 --> 00:07:00,962
I'M GOING TO GET HER
SOME FLOWERS.

181
00:07:00,962 --> 00:07:03,298
NOW, WHO WOULD NOT WANT
TO LIVE WITH ME?

182
00:07:03,298 --> 00:07:04,591
I DON'T.

183
00:07:04,591 --> 00:07:05,926
NO, I WANT TO LIVE

184
00:07:05,926 --> 00:07:08,845
WITH THE SUPER-HOT
AUSTRALIAN DANCER.

185
00:07:08,845 --> 00:07:10,097
OKAY, NOW,
HOW'S THAT GOING NOW?

186
00:07:10,097 --> 00:07:11,806
ARE YOU OKAY
WITH THE NOT-FLIRTING THING?

187
00:07:11,806 --> 00:07:14,351
UH, YEAH, BUT... SO FAR,
YEAH BUT IT'S TOUGH, YOU KNOW?

188
00:07:14,351 --> 00:07:16,686
I GOT ALL THIS-THIS
BUILT-UP FLIRTING ENERGY

189
00:07:16,686 --> 00:07:21,191
AND-AND I DON'T KNOW
HOW TO GET RID OF IT.

190
00:07:21,191 --> 00:07:23,235
HOW YOU DOIN'?

191
00:07:28,031 --> 00:07:31,201
( voice cracking ):
OH, MAN.

192
00:07:31,201 --> 00:07:33,161
SORRY, THERE'S JUST MORE ROOM
OUT HERE.

193
00:07:33,161 --> 00:07:36,331
OH, NO, NO, NO, IT'S-IT'S, UH...
YOU JUST, UH, UH, REMINDED ME

194
00:07:36,331 --> 00:07:39,418
THAT, UH, I HAVE
TO DO MY STRETCHES, TOO, YEAH.

195
00:07:43,422 --> 00:07:45,257
( groaning painfully )

196
00:07:45,257 --> 00:07:47,634
WHY DON'T YOU TRY TO...
( yelping )

197
00:07:47,634 --> 00:07:49,719
WHAT'S WRONG?
UH, UH, NOTHING.

198
00:07:49,719 --> 00:07:51,721
I JUST, UH...
I-I DIDN'T WANT YOU TO TOUCH ME

199
00:07:51,721 --> 00:07:53,181
BECAUSE I'M-I'M
ALL SWEATY

200
00:07:53,181 --> 00:07:55,142
FROM THE WORKOUT.

201
00:07:55,142 --> 00:07:56,726
I'M GOING TO HIT THE SHOWER.

202
00:08:00,063 --> 00:08:01,689
OH, MY GOD!

203
00:08:01,689 --> 00:08:03,691
OH, SORRY ABOUT THAT
STUFF HANGING IN THERE.

204
00:08:03,691 --> 00:08:07,279
IT'S JUST MY THONGS ARE
TOO DELICATE FOR THE DRYER.

205
00:08:07,279 --> 00:08:08,363
OH...

206
00:08:08,363 --> 00:08:10,449
( laughing nervously )

207
00:08:10,449 --> 00:08:13,201
( whimpering )

208
00:08:13,201 --> 00:08:15,162
( exhaling rhythmically )

209
00:08:18,165 --> 00:08:19,749
HI!
( startled yell )

210
00:08:19,749 --> 00:08:21,168
OH, YEAH, UH-HUH,
IT'S ME.

211
00:08:21,168 --> 00:08:23,044
I SAW YOU GRAB
YOUR RUNNING SHOES
THIS MORNING

212
00:08:23,044 --> 00:08:24,921
AND SNEAK OUT.

213
00:08:24,921 --> 00:08:26,714
YOU LIED
SO YOU COULD RUN
BY YOURSELF.

214
00:08:26,714 --> 00:08:28,842
NO, PHOEBE, NO,
I WAS... NO.
YOU KNOW WHAT?

215
00:08:28,842 --> 00:08:31,552
I WAS... I WAS ACTUALLY
JUST CHECKING...

216
00:08:31,552 --> 00:08:34,722
TO SEE... IF I
COULD RUN AND I CAN.

217
00:08:34,722 --> 00:08:36,850
PLEASE, RACHEL,
I AM NOT AN IDIOT.

218
00:08:36,850 --> 00:08:37,892
NO, WAIT, PHOEBE.

219
00:08:50,405 --> 00:08:52,324
WOW... COUPLES
WHO LIVE TOGETHER DO START

220
00:08:52,324 --> 00:08:55,243
TO LOOK ALIKE.

221
00:08:55,243 --> 00:08:57,412
SO... MON-DLER...

222
00:08:57,412 --> 00:08:58,621
UH...

223
00:08:59,873 --> 00:09:02,876
WHAT, UH... WH...
WHAT YOU DOING?

224
00:09:02,876 --> 00:09:05,295
WHAT DOES IT LOOK LIKE?
I AM CLEANING.

225
00:09:05,295 --> 00:09:06,880
DID YOU GET MONICA'S
AUTHORIZATION

226
00:09:06,880 --> 00:09:08,756
TO MOVE ALL
OF HER STUFF?

227
00:09:08,756 --> 00:09:09,966
"AUTHORIZATION"--
I DON'T NEED THAT.

228
00:09:09,966 --> 00:09:11,550
I'M GONNA
PUT EVERYTHING BACK.

229
00:09:11,550 --> 00:09:13,887
PUT IT BACK EXACTLY
WHERE YOU FOUND IT?

230
00:09:13,887 --> 00:09:17,682
YES, I'M GOING TO PUT IT BACK
"EXACTLY" WHERE I FOUND IT.

231
00:09:17,682 --> 00:09:19,976
OKAY, FIRST OF ALL, THAT
ATTITUDE IS NOT HELPING.

232
00:09:19,976 --> 00:09:21,853
OKAY, SHE IS NOT
GOING TO CARE

233
00:09:21,853 --> 00:09:24,022
IF I PUT HER STUFF BACK
IN THE SAME STUPID PLACE.

234
00:09:24,022 --> 00:09:28,568
OH, HELLO?
DID YOU JUST MEET MONICA?

235
00:09:28,568 --> 00:09:31,071
SHE'S GOING TO RECOGNIZE
THAT I DID A NICE THING

236
00:09:31,071 --> 00:09:33,740
AND-AND APPRECIATE IT.

237
00:09:33,740 --> 00:09:34,824
HUH.
YOU KNOW, ACTUALLY

238
00:09:34,824 --> 00:09:36,326
THIS WILL WORK OUT WELL

239
00:09:36,326 --> 00:09:38,495
BECAUSE WHEN YOU HAVE
TO MOVE BACK IN WITH JOEY

240
00:09:38,495 --> 00:09:41,789
JOEY'S HOT NEW ROOMMATE
CAN COME LIVE WITH ME.

241
00:09:41,789 --> 00:09:42,999
I SEE. I SEE.

242
00:09:42,999 --> 00:09:44,792
Y-Y-YOU'RE TRYING
TO FREAK ME OUT.

243
00:09:44,792 --> 00:09:48,171
LOOK, CHANDLER, MONICA
IS REALLY WEIRD

244
00:09:48,171 --> 00:09:49,548
ABOUT THIS KIND OF
STUFF, ALL RIGHT?

245
00:09:49,548 --> 00:09:51,674
BELIEVE ME, I LIVED
WITH HER FOR 16 YEARS.

246
00:09:51,674 --> 00:09:54,553
SHE IS GOING TO FREAK OUT.

247
00:09:54,553 --> 00:09:58,014
OH, MY GOD,
SHE'S GOING TO SIT ON YOU.

248
00:09:58,014 --> 00:09:59,182
NO, SHE'S NOT, OKAY?

249
00:09:59,182 --> 00:10:00,350
YOU KNOW,
I'LL PROVE IT TO YOU.

250
00:10:00,350 --> 00:10:03,728
I'M GOING
TO CALL HER RIGHT NOW.

251
00:10:03,728 --> 00:10:06,231
PHONE'S DONE.
( chuckles sarcastically )

252
00:10:07,815 --> 00:10:08,816
HEY, MON,
HOW'S IT GOING?

253
00:10:08,816 --> 00:10:10,402
Monica:
Terrible.

254
00:10:10,402 --> 00:10:11,945
I TELL YOU, IF-IF-IF I WANT
SOMETHING DONE RIGHT

255
00:10:11,945 --> 00:10:12,987
I HAVE TO DO IT MYSELF.

256
00:10:12,987 --> 00:10:16,575
Other people just wreck stuff.

257
00:10:16,575 --> 00:10:18,910
I REALLY THINK
I MIGHT KILL SOMEONE TONIGHT.

258
00:10:21,079 --> 00:10:23,206
OH, COME ON, COME ON,
IT CAN'T BE THAT BAD.

259
00:10:23,206 --> 00:10:24,374
IT'S WORSE.

260
00:10:24,374 --> 00:10:25,833
THE ONLY THING
GETTING ME THROUGH IS

261
00:10:25,833 --> 00:10:27,668
KNOWING I'M GONNA
BE SEEING YOU SOON.

262
00:10:27,668 --> 00:10:28,795
I think I might even try
to get out of here early.

263
00:10:28,795 --> 00:10:31,047
NO, NO, NO, NO, NO, NO, NO.

264
00:10:31,047 --> 00:10:33,007
NO, IT SOUNDS LIKE
THEY REALLY NEED YOU DOWN THERE.

265
00:10:33,007 --> 00:10:34,426
AREN'T YOU JUST
HANGING OUT WITH ROSS?

266
00:10:34,426 --> 00:10:36,386
IT'S ALL GOOD.
OKAY, BYE-BYE, MON.

267
00:10:38,763 --> 00:10:40,765
SH-SHE'S GOING TO KILL ME.

268
00:10:40,765 --> 00:10:43,935
YOU KNOW, THE PHONE WAS FACING
THE OTHER WAY...

269
00:10:43,935 --> 00:10:45,520
AND THAT GOES
BACK UP THERE.

270
00:10:50,233 --> 00:10:51,692
YOU KNOW WHAT WE SHOULD DO?
WE SHOULD START WITH
THE BIG STUFF,

271
00:10:51,692 --> 00:10:53,111
YOU KNOW?
THAT'LL BE THE EASIEST.

272
00:10:53,111 --> 00:10:55,822
SO, UH, LET'S START
WITH THE COUCH.

273
00:10:57,282 --> 00:11:02,370
I GOT IT.

274
00:11:02,370 --> 00:11:03,955
YEAH, THAT-THAT
DOESN'T LOOK RIGHT.

275
00:11:03,955 --> 00:11:05,457
WHAT ARE YOU TALKING ABOUT?

276
00:11:05,457 --> 00:11:07,459
THE COUCH IS PERFECTLY IN LINE
WITH THE CARPET

277
00:11:07,459 --> 00:11:09,043
AND THEN I COULD JUST
WALK OVER HERE

278
00:11:09,043 --> 00:11:11,379
AND CASUALLY JUST PUT
MY FEET RIGHT UP ON...

279
00:11:13,340 --> 00:11:15,342
OKAY, HERE'S WHAT WE DO--
WE JUST, UH,

280
00:11:15,342 --> 00:11:16,926
MOVE THE COUCH CLOSER
TO THE COFFEE TABLE.

281
00:11:16,926 --> 00:11:18,677
WHOA, YEAH, BUT THEN
THE BACK OF THE COUCH

282
00:11:18,677 --> 00:11:21,264
WON'T LINE UP WITH
THE BACK OF THE CARPET.

283
00:11:21,264 --> 00:11:23,141
OKAY, WELL, HERE--
WE'LL JUST, UH...

284
00:11:23,141 --> 00:11:25,726
WE'LL MOVE THE COFFEE TABLE
CLOSER TO THE COUCH.

285
00:11:25,726 --> 00:11:26,727
NO, WHOA! WHOA!

286
00:11:26,727 --> 00:11:28,062
BUT THEN THE COFFEE TABLE

287
00:11:28,062 --> 00:11:31,690
WON'T BE CENTERED
IN THE SEATING AREA.

288
00:11:31,690 --> 00:11:33,443
YES, BUT THE COFFEE TABLE
DOESN'T HAVE TO...

289
00:11:33,443 --> 00:11:37,322
( blubbering )
ROSS!

290
00:11:37,322 --> 00:11:40,617
ALL RIGHT, LOOK,
WHAT AM I GOING TO DO?

291
00:11:40,617 --> 00:11:42,869
I'M NOT FLIRTING, BUT STILL,
I'M-I'M DRAWING HER TO ME

292
00:11:42,869 --> 00:11:45,038
LIKE-LIKE-LIKE
A MOTH TO A FLAME!

293
00:11:50,251 --> 00:11:54,339
WHAT THE HELL'S
GOING ON OVER HERE?!

294
00:11:54,339 --> 00:11:55,798
MONICA'S GOING TO KILL YOU.

295
00:11:57,300 --> 00:11:58,759
LOOK, I NEED YOUR HELP, OKAY?

296
00:11:58,759 --> 00:12:02,763
I HAVE TO DO SOMETHING
TO-TO REPEL THIS WOMAN.

297
00:12:02,763 --> 00:12:04,723
WAIT A MINUTE, WAIT A MINUTE.

298
00:12:04,723 --> 00:12:07,977
YOU GUYS REPEL WOMEN
ALL THE TIME!

299
00:12:07,977 --> 00:12:10,021
HEY, I'VE BEEN MARRIED
THREE TIMES.

300
00:12:15,235 --> 00:12:16,236
NO, NO, NO, NO, NO!

301
00:12:16,236 --> 00:12:17,612
I'VE SEEN IT HAPPEN.

302
00:12:17,612 --> 00:12:19,738
YOU GET A RAPPORT GOING
WITH A WOMAN,

303
00:12:19,738 --> 00:12:22,075
BUT SOMEHOW YOU MANAGE
TO KILL IT.

304
00:12:23,284 --> 00:12:26,120
WHAT'S YOUR SECRET?

305
00:12:26,120 --> 00:12:28,789
LOOK, WE DO NOT
REPEL WOMEN, OKAY?

306
00:12:28,789 --> 00:12:30,875
THAT IS COMPLETELY UNTRUE.

307
00:12:30,875 --> 00:12:33,670
UH, YES, WE DO, MY MAN.

308
00:12:33,670 --> 00:12:34,921
REMEMBER WHEN WE WERE
BACK IN COLLEGE

309
00:12:34,921 --> 00:12:36,381
AND WE WENT
TO THAT SPRING DANCE

310
00:12:36,381 --> 00:12:38,258
AND YOU WALKED RIGHT UP
TO THAT GIRL YOU LIKED

311
00:12:38,258 --> 00:12:39,676
AND YOU COULD NOT
STOP TALKING ABOUT

312
00:12:39,676 --> 00:12:42,387
THE IRISH
POTATO FAMINE?

313
00:12:42,387 --> 00:12:43,930
WELL, WHAT ABOUT YOU?

314
00:12:43,930 --> 00:12:46,140
YOU WEREN'T SO, YOU KNOW,
HOT IN COLLEGE, EITHER.

315
00:12:46,140 --> 00:12:51,354
AFTER EVERYTHING HE SAID,
HE'D GO "BA-DUM-BUMP. CHSSH."

316
00:12:51,354 --> 00:12:52,855
YEAH, MONICA DOESN'T
LIKE THAT, EITHER.

317
00:12:52,855 --> 00:12:55,400
MAYBE I SHOULD STOP
DOING THAT.

318
00:12:55,400 --> 00:12:57,068
WELL, YOU KNOW WHAT?
GIRLS DON'T LIKE IT

319
00:12:57,068 --> 00:12:58,695
WHEN I START TALKING
ABOUT SCIENCE.

320
00:12:58,695 --> 00:13:02,031
THAT'S NOT SPECIFIC
TO GIRLS.

321
00:13:02,031 --> 00:13:03,157
THIS IS GREAT,
THIS IS GREAT!

322
00:13:03,157 --> 00:13:04,992
WHAT-WHAT ELSE,
WHAT ELSE?

323
00:13:04,992 --> 00:13:07,161
UH... OH, THEY DON'T LIKE IT
WHEN YOU CORRECT THEIR GRAMMAR.

324
00:13:07,161 --> 00:13:11,790
AND THEY DON'T LIKE IT
WHEN YOU EXPLAIN WHY
YOUR JOKES ARE FUNNY.

325
00:13:11,790 --> 00:13:13,792
YOU KNOW, THEY DON'T LIKE IT
WHEN YOU KEEP ASKING THEM

326
00:13:13,792 --> 00:13:16,546
IF THEY LIKE YOU.

327
00:13:16,546 --> 00:13:18,506
MAN, I AM SO LUCKY
I HAVE MONICA.

328
00:13:18,506 --> 00:13:20,550
I'M NEVER GOING TO
FIND LOVE AGAIN.

329
00:13:24,803 --> 00:13:27,014
HEY.
PHOEBE, CAN I TALK TO YOU
FOR A SECOND?

330
00:13:27,014 --> 00:13:28,433
SURE.

331
00:13:28,433 --> 00:13:34,606
OKAY, UM, I...
ALL RIGHT, PHOEBE, LOOK--

332
00:13:34,606 --> 00:13:37,191
I JUST WANTED TO SAY
THAT I'M SORRY, OKAY?

333
00:13:37,191 --> 00:13:39,944
I HANDLED THE SITUATION
HORRIBLY

334
00:13:39,944 --> 00:13:43,364
AND-AND I SHOULD NOT HAVE LIED
TO YOU.

335
00:13:43,364 --> 00:13:45,617
SO, WHAT SHOULD YOU HAVE DONE?

336
00:13:45,617 --> 00:13:47,702
WELL, I-I SHOULD HAVE
TOLD YOU THE TRUTH.

337
00:13:47,702 --> 00:13:48,787
UH-HUH...

338
00:13:48,787 --> 00:13:50,622
WHICH IS?

339
00:13:50,622 --> 00:13:52,373
WELL, YOU KNOW...

340
00:13:52,373 --> 00:13:56,210
THE REASON THAT I DIDN'T WANT
TO GO RUNNING WITH YOU IS

341
00:13:56,210 --> 00:13:58,797
BECAUSE, UH, WELL, YOU KNOW,
THE WAY THAT YOU RUN

342
00:13:58,797 --> 00:14:00,256
IS JUST A LITTLE...

343
00:14:03,510 --> 00:14:05,261
SO?
WELL, IT'S EMBARRASSING.

344
00:14:05,261 --> 00:14:07,472
PEOPLE WERE LOOKING AT US
LIKE WE WERE CRAZY.

345
00:14:07,472 --> 00:14:08,640
WHY DO YOU CARE?

346
00:14:08,640 --> 00:14:11,017
BECAUSE THEY'RE PEOPLE.

347
00:14:11,017 --> 00:14:13,770
BUT PEOPLE THAT YOU DON'T KNOW
AND WILL NEVER SEE AGAIN.

348
00:14:13,770 --> 00:14:16,314
YES, BUT STILL, THEY ARE
PEOPLE...

349
00:14:16,314 --> 00:14:19,066
WITH EYES.

350
00:14:19,066 --> 00:14:21,653
WELL, I DIDN'T GET EMBARRASSED
RUNNING NEXT TO MISS...

351
00:14:21,653 --> 00:14:22,987
( panting )

352
00:14:25,490 --> 00:14:27,074
BUT, OH, OKAY.

353
00:14:27,074 --> 00:14:29,243
NO, NO, I CAN SEE
WHY RUNNING WITH ME

354
00:14:29,243 --> 00:14:31,162
WOULD BE EMBARRASSING TO YOU.

355
00:14:31,162 --> 00:14:32,163
YEAH, OKAY.

356
00:14:32,163 --> 00:14:33,164
YOU'RE UPTIGHT.

357
00:14:33,164 --> 00:14:34,248
WH...!

358
00:14:34,248 --> 00:14:35,834
I... LIS...
I AM NOT UPTIGHT...

359
00:14:35,834 --> 00:14:37,752
( laughing ):
NO...

360
00:14:37,752 --> 00:14:39,962
LISTEN, I AM NOT...

361
00:14:39,962 --> 00:14:43,675
UPTIGHT, MAN.

362
00:14:43,675 --> 00:14:44,718
THAT'S OKAY, RACHEL.

363
00:14:44,718 --> 00:14:45,885
I'M NOT JUDGING YOU.

364
00:14:45,885 --> 00:14:47,554
THAT'S JUST WHO YOU ARE.

365
00:14:47,554 --> 00:14:48,887
ME, I'M MORE FREE,
YOU KNOW?

366
00:14:48,887 --> 00:14:51,015
I RUN LIKE I DID
WHEN I WAS A KID

367
00:14:51,015 --> 00:14:53,934
BECAUSE IT'S THE ONLY WAY
IT'S FUN, YOU KNOW?

368
00:14:53,934 --> 00:14:55,478
I MEAN, DIDN'T YOU EVER
RUN SO FAST

369
00:14:55,478 --> 00:14:57,438
YOU THOUGHT YOUR LEGS
WERE GOING TO FALL OFF?

370
00:14:57,438 --> 00:15:00,233
YOU KNOW, LIKE WHEN YOU WERE
RUNNING TOWARD THE SWINGS

371
00:15:00,233 --> 00:15:02,943
OR-OR RUNNING AWAY
FROM SATAN?

372
00:15:06,239 --> 00:15:07,657
THE NEIGHBORS' DOG.

373
00:15:07,657 --> 00:15:09,075
OH.

374
00:15:12,245 --> 00:15:14,038
OKAY, IS THIS LAMP
IN THE RIGHT PLACE?

375
00:15:14,038 --> 00:15:18,918
WHO CARES? I REPEL WOMEN.

376
00:15:18,918 --> 00:15:21,212
NO, NO, NO, NO, NO, NO!
YOU CAN'T COME IN HERE.

377
00:15:21,212 --> 00:15:23,089
R-R-ROSS IS NAKED!

378
00:15:25,550 --> 00:15:26,551
WHAT?!

379
00:15:26,551 --> 00:15:28,302
WHAT?!

380
00:15:28,302 --> 00:15:29,888
I COULDN'T SAY
THAT I WAS NAKED

381
00:15:29,888 --> 00:15:31,930
BECAUSE SHE'S ALLOWED
TO SEE ME NAKED.

382
00:15:31,930 --> 00:15:34,517
WHY DOES ANYONE
HAVE TO BE NAKED?

383
00:15:36,561 --> 00:15:39,272
WHY IS ROSS NAKED?

384
00:15:41,148 --> 00:15:45,820
I... I HAD TO...
SHOW CHANDLER SOMETHING.

385
00:15:48,072 --> 00:15:50,283
NAKED?

386
00:15:50,283 --> 00:15:51,868
YEAH, I-I, UH...

387
00:15:51,868 --> 00:15:54,412
I GUESS I HAVE A, UH...

388
00:15:54,412 --> 00:15:57,874
A GUY PROBLEM.

389
00:15:57,874 --> 00:15:59,959
IS IT THE SAME THING
THAT CHANDLER HAD?

390
00:16:04,088 --> 00:16:05,715
LOOK, UH, JUST-JUST
COME BACK LATER.

391
00:16:05,715 --> 00:16:06,925
WE'LL GET EVERYTHING
SQUARED AWAY

392
00:16:06,925 --> 00:16:08,968
AND YOU CAN COME BACK LATER.
OKAY.

393
00:16:08,968 --> 00:16:11,095
HEY, LISTEN, THERE'S STILL SOME
OF CHANDLER'S MEDICINE LEFT

394
00:16:11,095 --> 00:16:14,724
UNDER THE SINK IN
THE BATHROOM. BYE.

395
00:16:14,724 --> 00:16:15,683
BYE-BYE.

396
00:16:21,522 --> 00:16:22,941
THANK GOD.

397
00:16:26,277 --> 00:16:27,695
DUDE, WHAT'D YOU HAVE?

398
00:16:29,781 --> 00:16:31,825
LOOK, WE HAVE NO TIME, OKAY?

399
00:16:31,825 --> 00:16:33,785
WE MUST FOCUS.
WE GOT TO GET EVERYTHING BACK

400
00:16:33,785 --> 00:16:36,996
INTO ITS
ORIGINAL PLACE.
THE PHOTO ALBUM.

401
00:16:36,996 --> 00:16:40,750
THERE WERE MILLIONS OF
PICTURES OF THE APARTMENT
IN THE PHOTO ALBUM.

402
00:16:40,750 --> 00:16:43,753
WE JUST GO THROUGH IT AND MATCH
EVERYTHING TO THE PICTURES.

403
00:16:43,753 --> 00:16:44,754
THAT'S PERFECT.

404
00:16:44,754 --> 00:16:46,005
THAT'S BRILLIANT.

405
00:16:49,175 --> 00:16:53,680
SO, REALLY,
WHAT'D YOU HAVE?

406
00:16:53,680 --> 00:16:57,016
HEY, JOEY, I GOT
SOME BEER FOR YOU.

407
00:16:57,016 --> 00:17:02,188
UH, DON'T-DON'T YOU MEAN,
"FOR WHOM"?

408
00:17:02,188 --> 00:17:04,357
SURE.

409
00:17:04,357 --> 00:17:05,650
LISTEN, I WAS GOING TO ORDER
SOME PIZZA.

410
00:17:05,650 --> 00:17:07,485
YOU WANT TO SHARE ONE?

411
00:17:07,485 --> 00:17:09,696
PIZZA? HA! IT'S NOT LIKE
I'VE NEVER HAD THAT BEFORE.

412
00:17:09,696 --> 00:17:11,197
BA-DUM-BUMP. CHSSH.

413
00:17:14,032 --> 00:17:16,703
IS THERE SOMETHING WRONG?

414
00:17:16,703 --> 00:17:18,663
ALL RIGHT, ALL RIGHT.

415
00:17:18,663 --> 00:17:21,958
LET'S JUST GET THIS OUT
IN THE OPEN, OKAY?

416
00:17:21,958 --> 00:17:22,959
YOU'RE HOT.

417
00:17:24,460 --> 00:17:26,629
I'M LOVABLE.

418
00:17:26,629 --> 00:17:29,382
CLEARLY, THERE'S A VIBE
GOING ON BETWEEN US

419
00:17:29,382 --> 00:17:31,843
BUT WE'RE ROOMMATES

420
00:17:31,843 --> 00:17:35,596
AND IT'S A HUGE MISTAKE FOR US
TO CONTINUE DOWN THIS ROAD.

421
00:17:35,596 --> 00:17:37,557
JOEY...
NO, NO, NO, I'M TELLING YOU.

422
00:17:37,557 --> 00:17:39,559
IMAGINE YOURSELF
LIVING IN A SUPERMARKET

423
00:17:39,559 --> 00:17:43,103
AND YOU WILL
UNDERSTAND.

424
00:17:43,103 --> 00:17:47,066
OKAY, SO THE QUESTION IS,
WHAT DO WE DO?

425
00:17:47,066 --> 00:17:49,151
WELL, I DON'T THINK
THERE IS ANYTHING TO DO.

426
00:17:49,151 --> 00:17:51,487
I MEAN, I THINK
YOU'RE REALLY SWEET

427
00:17:51,487 --> 00:17:54,365
BUT I'M JUST NOT INTERESTED
IN YOU LIKE THAT.

428
00:17:58,995 --> 00:18:02,749
OH!
NO, I MEAN...

429
00:18:02,749 --> 00:18:04,834
( sighing ):
YOU'RE A REALLY NICE GUY

430
00:18:04,834 --> 00:18:06,961
AND I'M HAPPY TO BE
YOUR ROOMMATE

431
00:18:06,961 --> 00:18:09,547
AND YOUR FRIEND.
I'M JUST...

432
00:18:09,547 --> 00:18:14,510
YOU KNOW, I JUST DON'T
FEEL THAT WAY ABOUT YOU.

433
00:18:14,510 --> 00:18:19,223
OH... I SEE WHAT HAPPENED.
( laughing )

434
00:18:19,223 --> 00:18:22,602
IT'S BECAUSE I WAS TRYING
TO REPEL YOU, RIGHT?

435
00:18:22,602 --> 00:18:28,274
BELIEVE ME, YOU'D FEEL A LOT
DIFFERENT IF I TURNED IT ON.

436
00:18:28,274 --> 00:18:30,651
I DON'T THINK SO.
OH, I DO.

437
00:18:33,446 --> 00:18:35,823
HOW YOU DOIN'?

438
00:18:37,450 --> 00:18:39,744
I'M OKAY.

439
00:18:39,744 --> 00:18:42,120
WHAT?

440
00:18:42,120 --> 00:18:44,123
WHAT?

441
00:18:44,123 --> 00:18:46,166
OH, DEAR GOD!

442
00:18:51,297 --> 00:18:54,050
( panting )

443
00:19:03,851 --> 00:19:04,894
( both screaming )

444
00:19:04,894 --> 00:19:05,937
HEY!
HEY!

445
00:19:05,937 --> 00:19:06,980
PHEEBS!

446
00:19:06,980 --> 00:19:08,773
OH, HONEY, I'M SO SORRY.

447
00:19:08,773 --> 00:19:10,316
YOU WERE RIGHT--
THIS FEELS GREAT!

448
00:19:10,316 --> 00:19:12,276
SEE? AND YOU DON'T CARE
IF PEOPLE ARE STARING.

449
00:19:12,276 --> 00:19:14,194
IT'S JUST FOR A SECOND,
'CAUSE THEN YOU'RE GONE!

450
00:19:14,194 --> 00:19:15,321
GONE!

451
00:19:15,321 --> 00:19:16,614
I MEAN, IT'S AMAZING, PHEEBS!

452
00:19:16,614 --> 00:19:19,075
I FEEL SO FREE,
AND SO GRACEFUL...

453
00:19:19,075 --> 00:19:20,076
AAH!

454
00:19:23,663 --> 00:19:26,248
HEY! LOOK OUT FOR THE HORSE.

455
00:19:26,248 --> 00:19:27,249
SORRY.

456
00:19:32,546 --> 00:19:34,924
IS IT OKAY FOR ME
TO COME IN NOW?

457
00:19:34,924 --> 00:19:36,843
UH-HUH.

458
00:19:42,807 --> 00:19:44,100
WHY IS EVERYTHING DIFFERENT?

459
00:19:44,100 --> 00:19:45,225
BYE.

460
00:19:48,312 --> 00:19:50,023
NO, I DON'T SEE
ANYTHING DIFFERENT

461
00:19:50,023 --> 00:19:52,232
OTHER THAN THE FACT THAT THE
ROOM GOT SO MUCH BRIGHTER

462
00:19:52,232 --> 00:19:53,442
WHEN YOU CAME INTO IT.

463
00:19:53,442 --> 00:19:55,194
( forced laugh )

464
